From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=81ngel=20Ren=C3=A9?=
 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:47:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: raise the MFC clock while it is in use on MFC
 v15
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The bootloader leaves the Pixel 7's MFC at 100 MHz. Decoding only, that
gives about 22 fps for 3840x2160 H.264 and 64 fps for 1080p, so 4K
cannot play in real time.

On gs201 the MFC rate is a DVFS domain of the ACPM firmware, which sets
the voltage along with it. Let a variant name the rate to ask of its
first clock while the MFC is powered on, and put the previous rate back
at power off. MFC v15 asks for 666 MHz, the top of Google's gs201
mfc_freqs table.

On the Pixel 7, with the clock below in the device tree: the rate reads
666 MHz while decoding and 100 MHz again afterwards; decoding only, the
4K clip runs at about 70 fps and the 1080p one at about 280 fps; the 4K
clip plays on screen through glimagesink at 30 fps with no frame
dropped (44 shown and 72 dropped before); and the 300 4K frames and the
1800 frames of a 60 s 1080p clip match FFmpeg's software decoder bit
for bit.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c  |  2 ++
 .../platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h |  2 ++
 .../platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_pm.c     | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
index 21133072d..f06098227 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
@@ -1772,6 +1772,8 @@ static const struct s5p_mfc_variant mfc_drvdata_v15 = {
 	.clk_names	= {"mfc"},
 	.num_clocks	= 1,
 	.clocks_optional = true,
+	/* The top MFC rate of Google's gs201 tables (mfc_freqs) */
+	.active_clk_rate = 666000000,
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id exynos_mfc_match[] = {
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h
index 98ab487bd..a10cc406c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_common.h
@@ -199,6 +199,7 @@ struct s5p_mfc_pm {
 	struct clk	*clocks[MFC_MAX_CLOCKS];
 	int		num_clocks;
 	bool		use_clock_gating;
+	unsigned long	idle_clk_rate;
 
 	struct device	*device;
 };
@@ -235,6 +236,7 @@ struct s5p_mfc_variant {
 	int		num_clocks;
 	bool		use_clock_gating;
 	bool		clocks_optional;
+	unsigned long	active_clk_rate;
 };
 
 /**
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_pm.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_pm.c
index d60a04b5a..47107b16c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_pm.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_pm.c
@@ -84,6 +84,20 @@ int s5p_mfc_power_on(struct s5p_mfc_dev *dev)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Run at the variant's rate while the MFC is in use. The bootloader
+	 * leaves the GS201 MFC at 100 MHz, a quarter of what 4K needs.
+	 */
+	if (dev->variant->active_clk_rate && dev->pm.clocks[0]) {
+		dev->pm.idle_clk_rate = clk_get_rate(dev->pm.clocks[0]);
+		ret = clk_set_rate(dev->pm.clocks[0],
+				   dev->variant->active_clk_rate);
+		if (ret)
+			mfc_err("Failed to set the MFC clock to %lu Hz: %d\n",
+				dev->variant->active_clk_rate, ret);
+		ret = 0;
+	}
+
 	/* prepare for software clock gating */
 	clk_disable(dev->pm.clock_gate);
 
@@ -102,6 +116,11 @@ int s5p_mfc_power_off(struct s5p_mfc_dev *dev)
 	/* finish software clock gating */
 	clk_enable(dev->pm.clock_gate);
 
+	if (dev->pm.idle_clk_rate) {
+		clk_set_rate(dev->pm.clocks[0], dev->pm.idle_clk_rate);
+		dev->pm.idle_clk_rate = 0;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < dev->pm.num_clocks; i++)
 		clk_disable_unprepare(dev->pm.clocks[i]);
 
